- `ref(db, 'path')` - Create reference to path
- `set(ref, data)` - Write data (overwrites)
- `get(ref)` - Read once (returns promise)
- `update(ref, data)` - Partial update (merge)
- `remove(ref)` - Delete data
- `onValue(ref, callback, errorCallback)` - Real-time listener
- `push(ref)` - Generate new child with unique key
- `onDisconnect(ref)` - Handle disconnection cleanup

---

### 4. **Firebase onValue Listener Pattern** - Examples from Hooks

#### **useCompetitions.js** (Lines 383-395)
```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  const competitionsRef = ref(db, 'competitions');

  const unsubscribe = onValue(competitionsRef, (snapshot) => {
    setCompetitions(snapshot.val() || {});
    setLoading(false);
  }, (err) => {
    setError(err.message);
    setLoading(false);
